                                                    PROJECT REPORT – 2
                                    Travel Booking Platform Using Agile Methodology
1. Introduction

The Travel Booking Platform is a web-based application designed to help users search, plan, and book travel services such as trips, accommodations, and itineraries online. The platform provides a simple and user-friendly interface that allows customers to manage their travel plans efficiently.

This project is developed using the Agile Methodology, which ensures flexibility, faster development, and continuous improvement through iterative delivery of features.

2. Problem Statement

Traditional travel booking methods involve multiple agents, manual coordination, and lack of transparency in pricing and availability. Customers often face difficulties in comparing options and managing bookings. There is a need for an automated travel booking platform that offers reliable, fast, and centralized booking services.

3. Objectives of the Project

To provide an online travel booking solution
To simplify trip planning and booking
To reduce manual intervention and errors
To offer real-time booking management
To enhance customer experience

4. Scope of the Project

The platform supports user registration, travel search, booking management, and trip history tracking. Administrators can manage travel packages, monitor bookings, and maintain platform data.

5. Agile Methodology

Agile methodology focuses on iterative development, customer collaboration, and adaptability. The Travel Booking Platform is developed in multiple sprints, with each sprint delivering functional travel-related features.

Agile Practices Followed

Incremental development
Continuous testing
Regular feedback from users
Adaptive planning

